course: dictionary
lesson: 6516
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. A capital letter is one clue. Nelson with a small n usually means a wrestling hold, while Nelson with a capital N is usually a person's name or a place. «He was caught in a half nelson and could not move his arm.» Words like wrestling and move show that this is the hold.
explain: Other words around the name give clues too. «Nelson Mandela spent 27 years in prison under apartheid, South Africa's laws separating people by race, then became president in 1994.» Prison and president tell you Nelson is a person's name here. Ask: what would fit in this place? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some names are for places or things, not people. Nelson's Column is a monument in London, and Nelson is also a city in New Zealand. Look at the words beside the name, such as Trafalgar Square or the sea, to decide which Nelson the writer means.
fact: A nelson is a hold in wrestling: you put your arm under your opponent's arm and push on the back of their neck.
fact: A full nelson uses both arms, and a half nelson uses one arm.
fact: «Nelson Mandela was released in 1990 after 27 years in prison and elected president in 1994 in South Africa's first election open to all races.» Here Nelson is a first name.
fact: Admiral Horatio Nelson was a famous British naval hero, and Nelson's Column stands in Trafalgar Square, London.
fact: Nelson is also a city in New Zealand, and in cricket a score of 111 is called a «Nelson», which some fans think is unlucky.
exercise: «He put a full nelson on his opponent in the wrestling match.» What is a full nelson? | A cricket score of 111 | A city in New Zealand | A famous monument in London | *A wrestling hold using both arms
exercise: «Nelson Mandela was elected president in 1994.» In this sentence, Nelson is a | A city | A wrestling hold | *A person's name | A cricket score
exercise: Ella sees «Nelson's Column» in London. What is it? | *A tall monument in Trafalgar Square | A cricket score | A wrestling hold | A city in New Zealand
test: «He was caught in a half nelson.» What does nelson mean here? | *A wrestling hold using one arm | A famous admiral | A cricket score | A city
test: Which word in «Nelson Mandela spent 27 years in prison» tells you Nelson is a person? | *Mandela | spent | years | prison
exam: Jayden reads «The city of Nelson sits by the sea in New Zealand» and asks what Nelson means. Which answer is right? | *A city in New Zealand | A kind of sandwich | A wrestling hold | A cricket score of 111
